<title>USA: Regulations hinder cargo service growth in Asia.</title>
<headline>Regulations hinder cargo service growth in Asia.</headline>
<byline>Jessica Hall</byline>
<dateline>PHOENIX 1997-04-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Regulatory hurdles in Asia restrict cargo carriers from transporting goods between two foreign nations, inflate prices and limit service, air cargo executives said.</p>
<p>&quot;Protectionist aviation regimes curtail competition, growth and innovation, while denying consumers and communities the opportunity for better and more frequent service, lower pricing and improved quality,&quot; Bruce Barash, a regional vice president for MSAS Cargo International, said at the Sixth Annual Phoenix International Aviation Symposium.</p>
</text>
